<rml>
<head>
    <title>Debugging</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="tokens.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="case.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="mark.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="window.rcss"/>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="scrim" id="debug-scrim">
        <div class="case">

            <div class="lid stacked">
                <div class="lid-top">
                    <div class="head">
                        <div class="mark"></div>
                        <div class="title">Debugging</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="chrome">
                        <div class="win-btn" id="modal-close"><div class="glyph-x"><div class="bar a"></div><div class="bar b"></div></div></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="hint">For development, not for playing. Up and down to move, left and right to change, Escape or the pad's B goes back</div>
            </div>

            <!-- EVERYTHING MEANT FOR DEVELOPMENT RATHER THAN FOR PLAYING, in one place (the user,
                 2026-09-26). The rows are built by the shell from the same two models the other
                 menus use, picked out by key (is_debug_setting, is_debug_lighting in
                 ui_shell.cpp), so a row can never appear in both menus or in neither. The way in
                 is a confirmation, never this document directly. -->
            <div class="rows long" id="debug-rows"></div>

            <div class="foot">
                <span>Saved as you change it</span>
                <span id="debug-foot">Put anything you change back when you are done; none of this is needed to play</span>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
